          <div class="callout"><strong>Why Opus here:</strong> Over-merging at the cluster stage causes irreversible information loss — the global synthesis agents can only see what the clusterer passes. If two distinct concepts are collapsed here, they cannot be recovered. Opus errs toward finer-grained clusters. Under-clustering is recoverable; over-merging is not.</div>
